[Music]  abolishing the gender ministry  prosecuting women who made false  accusations of sex crimes  blaming south korea's low birth rate on  feminism  these are some of the pledges south  korea's new president yoon sagar has  made to gain male voters  [Music]  fighting against him is 26 year old pak  tihan  [Music]  park made a name for herself as an  activist who helped uncover a harrowing  digital sex crime network on telegram  offering images and videos of women in  humiliating and degrading poses or  videos of women harming themselves  we found chat rooms called the nth room  in july 2019 we spent five to six hours  every day collecting evidence scrolling  through these chat rooms  she was in journalism school and with a  classmate began an investigative project  into the online exploitation of women  they ended up bringing down the nth room  their investigation became the subject  of a netflix documentary called cyber  hell  pac revealed her identity in january and  became a senior advisor to the liberal  party's candidate for president  [Music]  i was afraid of the consequences of  revealing my identity i feared would my  family be okay but after two years of  activism i realized that my voice was  dwindling  since then she's emerged as a fiery  opponent president yun who swept into  office on a wave of anti-feminist  rhetoric and his gender split strategy  there's a huge gap between women and men  on how they perceive feminism and it's a  shame politicians used it in the  election  she's now the co-chair of the democratic  party  it's remarkable that a woman in her 20s  is the leader of the main opposition  party in korea but when i see a movement  to limit and reduce me to only gender  issues i want to tell them this is not a  gender issue it's a social issue  i think in south korea there's this  really unhappy collision of a society  which is incredibly technologically  advanced with super fast internet speeds  super high rates of smartphone ownership  with a country which is really lagging  behind on gender equality and so i think  that when you have that combination of  factors it's kind of combustible as far  as women's safety online and the ways in  which technology are used to further  abuse women  the risks exist in both virtual and real  life fueled by an unusual proliferation  of illegal videos taken by micro cameras  which come in various hidden forms  ranging from glasses to car keys  over 10 000 cases of digital sex crime  were reported in 2021 and 21.5 percent  of them had to do with illegal filming  it's too easy to commit a digital sex  crime there are people online who have  accumulated wealth by buying selling and  sharing these illegally filmed photos  and videos for decades there were also  cases where they said that they would  erase these things that they were  digital morticians and take money from  the victims to erase them this all  together has become a cartel  of those convicted of digital sex crimes  between 2016 and 2020 more than 81  percent have only received suspended  sentence or a fine  and just 9.4 percent were sentenced to  jail time of those imprisoned 82 percent  received less than 10 months  the legal system shouldn't just be about  prosecuting people it should also be  offering options to people like going to  court to get an order to say that  someone who has an image is ordered not  to share it or is ordered to destroy it  it should also be possible to go to  court and ask for damages  [Music]  there is an urgent need for a discussion  between the government and the police on  how to deal with sexual exploitation and  the sharing of these materials  experts say one of the reasons behind  what is animating the party of men  involved in any sort of digital sex  crime comes from pervasive misogyny in  korean culture  i think one of the ways that you see  that play out is that it seems quite  socially acceptable to a lot of people  in south korea to a lot of men and boys  to consume these images to create these  images is kind of seen by some men as a  kind of fun sort of male bonding rather  than being seen as gender-based violence  which is what it is  park faces an uphill battle men hold  more than a whopping 81 percent of  parliamentary seats in south korea  i saw a lot of sexual comments about me  that i wouldn't have gotten if i were a  man if i don't deal with them now it  would happen to another female  politician in her twenties i hope we can  grow into a society that guarantees more  diversity regardless of generation and  gender  [Music]

